# ====================
# Project Specific
# ====================

# Claude Code working state (keep shared commands, learnings, and the Judge
# Protocol infrastructure — agents, guard hook, hook wiring; ignore the rest)
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/LEARNINGS.md
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/ledger/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/workflows/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/team-engine.js
!.claude/team-engine.test.js
.claude/hooks/guard-log.txt
.claude/hooks/team-gate-log.txt
# The tracker's database. Binary, rewritten on every agent write, and its
# WAL/shm siblings churn constantly. The SCHEMA is version-controlled in
# .claude/ledger/track.py; the rows are this machine's run, not history.
.claude/ledger/tracker.db
.claude/ledger/tracker.db-wal
.claude/ledger/tracker.db-shm

# Keep .env.example and .env.test.example but ignore .env and .env.test
!.env.example
.env.test
!.env.test.example
.env.local
.env.cloud
# Generated audio files (local TTS output)
audio_store/

# Beat dedup review reports — intermediate human-review artifacts.
# Keep _log.jsonl tracked as audit trail; exclude per-run markdown reports.
data/*/_dedup_review/*.md
!data/*/_dedup_review/_log.jsonl

# Source-text PDFs under Books/ are large copyrighted third-party
# materials (50+ MB each, 200+ MB total). The chunked plain-text
# extracts under Books/{city}/{book-slug}/ are the canonical
# pipeline input and remain tracked.
Books/**/*.pdf

# Playwright test screenshots and reports
tests/reports/

# Local sandbox copy of Paris pipeline data — not referenced by tests or scripts.
data/paris_test/

# uv.lock is committed (reproducible dependency resolution)
# Do NOT add uv.lock to this file.

# Valhalla OSM extracts + built tiles (multi-GB, machine-local; make valhalla-build-tiles)
valhalla/custom_files/
.claude/hooks/guard-log.txt

# Scratch tour artifacts (make tour-build / measure-governor output) — machine-local
# reproduction output, never committed. Keeping them ignored removes the recurring
# "git add -A sweeps the scratch corpus into a commit" trap.
data/*/tours/

# Paid evaluator receipts are local audit/runtime state, never source or fixtures.
# Keep the authored tour batch (`tour-batch-v1`) visible for regression tests.
data/certification/tour-batch-review-v*/

# One-off paid text-candidate runs are local runtime/audit state. The checked
# regression corpus lives in `data/certification/tour-batch-v1` instead.
data/certification/*/text-candidate-*/

# Paid authoring reservation markers are resumability state, not regression fixtures.
data/certification/tour-batch-v*/**/attempt-*.json

# Superseded copies of a certification batch. Kept 'just in case' after a re-run,
# read by nothing, and indistinguishable from the live corpus by filename — the
# only thing that separates them is this rule.
data/certification/*-superseded-*/

# Vendored third-party skill bundles dropped in by tooling. Not this project's
# code, carry their own licences, and 146 files would otherwise be swept in by
# any `git add -A`.
.agents/

# Plans and specs are the agent's own scratch and are not part of a production
# launch. Owner ruling 2026-09-02: the directory was deleted and must never be
# committed again. `specs/` is also a `forbidden` prefix in
# .claude/hooks/production-junk-patterns.json, checked BEFORE the acknowledge
# token, so unlike every other rule here it cannot be waived by appending a word
# to a command. A /team run writes its context to `.claude/runs/{date}-{slug}`,
# already excluded by the `.claude/*` rule above.
#
# ANCHORED, with the leading slash. `specs/` on its own matches a directory at
# any depth, and this repo has already shipped that defect twice — an unanchored
# `models/` silently excluded src/api/models/ and mobile/lib/models/, real
# product source (see the `/models/` rule below, which carries the same scar).
# A third would be a pattern.
#
# Fourteen `!specs/...` exceptions used to sit here, because shipping code
# OPENED nine files inside those folders. All nine moved to `fixtures/` on
# 2026-09-02. Six were named by a path constant in source, and those constants
# were repointed. The other three were named inside a sealed JSON manifest and
# reached through it — invisible to any search over source code, and found only
# when the full suite went red on them. tests/test_fixture_constants_resolve.py
# now covers both kinds: it checks the six constants directly, and it walks the
# manifest the way the product does to reach the other three.
/specs/

# graphify's codebase map: 50MB of generated chunks, regenerated by the graphify
# skill. graph.json and GRAPH_REPORT.md are read by tooling from the working
# copy; nothing here belongs in history.
graphify-out/

# CodeGraph's SQLite index of this workspace, plus the self-ignoring stub it
# writes inside itself. Regenerated by the indexer from the working copy; the
# product does not read it and nothing that builds, tests or ships names it.
.codegraph/

# Local TTS model weights (fetched by preflight; never committed — 337MB).
# Anchored: an unanchored `models/` also silently excluded src/api/models/ and
# mobile/lib/models/ — real product source, tracked only because it predated
# this rule and would have been lost on any fresh add.
/models/

# The city pipeline's own run state and audit reports. The pipeline marks these
# with a leading dot — .pipeline-state, .pipeline-results, .area-classify,
# .batch-results, .gravity-*, .poi_research_batch_*, .upload-report-* — to keep
# its scratch separate from the corpus sitting beside it. 106 of them ended up
# tracked anyway. They are resume markers and one-off reports, never input: a
# fresh clone runs the pipeline identically without them.
data/*/.*
